\s1 A Call to Rebuild the Temple
\r (\ref Ezra 5:1–5|EZR 5:1-5\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the second|שְׁתַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the reign|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Darius|לְדָרְיָ֣וֶשׁ\rb*, \rb on the first|אֶחָ֖ד\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֣י\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֤ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שְׁאַלְתִּיאֵל֙\rb*, \rb governor|פַּחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֧עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehozadak|יְהוֹצָדָ֛ק\rb*,\f + \fr 1:1 \fqa Jehozadak \ft is a variant of \fqa Jozadak\ft ; also in verses 12 and 14; see \ref Ezra 3:2|EZR 3:2\ref*.\f* \rb the high|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֥ן\rb*, \rb stating|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb These|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אָֽמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb The time|עֶת־\rb* \rb has not yet|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb come|בֹּ֛א\rb*\rb |עֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb to rebuild|לְהִבָּנֽוֹת׃פ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.’”
\p \v 3 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֥י\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 4 “\rb Is it a time|הַעֵ֤ת\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb yourselves|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb to live|לָשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb in your paneled|סְפוּנִ֑ים\rb* \rb houses|בְּבָתֵּיכֶ֣ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb while this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb house|וְהַבַּ֥יִת\rb* \rb lies in ruins|חָרֵֽב׃\rb*?”
\p \v 5 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Consider carefully|שִׂ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |לְבַבְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your ways|דַּרְכֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb You have planted|זְרַעְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb much|הַרְבֵּ֜ה\rb*
\q2 \rb but harvested|וְהָבֵ֣א\rb* \rb little|מְעָ֗ט\rb*.
\q1 \rb You eat|אָכ֤וֹל\rb* \rb but never|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb have enough|לְשָׂבְעָה֙\rb*.
\q2 \rb You drink|שָׁת֣וֹ\rb* \rb but never|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb have your fill|לְשָׁכְרָ֔ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb You put on clothes|לָב֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb but never|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb get warm|לְחֹ֣ם\rb*.
\q2 \rb You earn wages|וְהַ֨מִּשְׂתַּכֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |מִשְׂתַּכֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to put into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a bag|צְר֥וֹר\rb* \rb pierced through|נָקֽוּב׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Consider carefully|שִׂ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |לְבַבְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your ways|דַּרְכֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Go up|עֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb into the hills|הָהָ֛ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb bring down|וַהֲבֵאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb lumber|עֵ֖ץ\rb*, \rb and build|וּבְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb the house|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*,
\q1 \rb so that I may take pleasure|וְאֶרְצֶה־\rb* \rb in it|בּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb and be glorified|וְאֶכָּבֵד\rb*,
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb You expected|פָּנֹ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb much|הַרְבֵּה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb but behold|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb it amounted to little|לִמְעָ֔ט\rb*.
\q1 \rb And what you brought|וַהֲבֵאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb home|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*, \rb I blew away|וְנָפַ֣חְתִּי\rb*.
\q2 \rb Why|יַ֣עַן\rb*\rb |מֶ֗ה\rb*? \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \rb Because|יַ֗עַן\rb* \rb My house|בֵּיתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb still lies in ruins|חָרֵ֔ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb while each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of you|וְאַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb is busy|רָצִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb with his own house|לְבֵיתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*,\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb on account of you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb the heavens|שָמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb have withheld|כָּלְא֥וּ\rb* \rb their dew|מִטָּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and the earth|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb has withheld|כָּלְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb its crops|יְבוּלָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb I have summoned|וָאֶקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb a drought|חֹ֜רֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the fields|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶהָרִ֗ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the grain|הַדָּגָן֙\rb*, \rb new wine|הַתִּיר֣וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb oil|הַיִּצְהָ֔ר\rb*,\rb |וְעַ֛ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and on whatever|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the ground|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb yields|תּוֹצִ֖יא\rb*,
\q1 \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and beast|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and on|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the labor|יְגִ֥יעַ\rb* \rb of your hands|כַּפָּֽיִם׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 The People Obey
\p \v 12 \rb Then Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֣ל׀\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שַׁלְתִּיאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb and Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehozadak|יְהוֹצָדָק֩\rb*, \rb the high|הַגָּד֜וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֨ן\rb*, \rb as well as all|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*, \rb obeyed|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the voice|בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֣י\rb*, \rb because|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb had sent him|שְׁלָח֖וֹ\rb*. \rb So the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb feared|וַיִּֽירְא֥וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֞י\rb*, \rb the messenger|מַלְאַ֧ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb delivered|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb the message|בְּמַלְאֲכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the people|לָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb I am|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb*,”
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stirred|וַיָּ֣עַר\rb* \rb the spirit|רוּחַ֩\rb* \rb of Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֨ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שַׁלְתִּיאֵ֜ל\rb*, \rb governor|פַּחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֙וּחַ֙\rb* \rb of Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehozadak|יְהוֹצָדָק֙\rb*, \rb the high|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb as well as|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb of all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*. \rb And they came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and|וַיַּעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb began the work|מְלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb*, \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*, \v 15 \rb on the twenty-fourth|עֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֛ה\rb* \rb day|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb of the sixth|בַּשִּׁשִּׁ֑י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb in the second|שְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb Darius|לְדָרְיָ֥וֶשׁ\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 The Coming Glory of God’s House
\p \v 1 \rb On the twenty-first day|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb of the seventh|בַּשְּׁבִיעִ֕י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֥י\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 2 “\rb Speak|אֱמָר־\rb*\rb |נָ֗א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֤ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שַׁלְתִּיאֵל֙\rb*, \rb governor|פַּחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehozadak|יְהוֹצָדָ֖ק\rb*,\f + \fr 2:2 \fqa Jehozadak \ft is a variant of \fqa Jozadak\ft ; also in verse 4; see \ref Ezra 3:2|EZR 3:2\ref*.\f* \rb the high|הַגָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb and also to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*. \rb Ask them|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 3 ‘\rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb is left|הַנִּשְׁאָ֔ר\rb* \rb among you|בָכֶם֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb saw|רָאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb in its former|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb glory|בִּכְבוֹד֖וֹ\rb*? \rb How|וּמָ֨ה\rb* \rb does it look|רֹאִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb now|עַ֔תָּה\rb*? \rb Does it not|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb appear to you|בְּעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb like nothing|כְּאַ֖יִן\rb* \rb in comparison|כָמֹ֛הוּ\rb*?’
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb be strong|חֲזַ֣ק\rb*, \rb O Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֣ל׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Be strong|וַחֲזַ֣ק\rb*, \rb O Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehozadak|יְהוֹצָדָק֩\rb*,
\q2 \rb the high|הַגָּד֜וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֨ן\rb*.
\q1 \rb And be strong|וַחֲזַ֨ק\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Work|וַֽעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*! \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am with you|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb This is the promise|הַדָּבָ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I made|כָּרַ֤תִּי\rb* \rb to you|אִתְּכֶם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb when you came out|בְּצֵאתְכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb*.
\q1 \rb And My Spirit|וְרוּחִ֖י\rb* \rb remains|עֹמֶ֣דֶת\rb* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכְכֶ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָֽאוּ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Once|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb more|ע֥וֹד\rb*, \rb in a little while|מְעַ֣ט\rb*,\rb |הִ֑יא\rb*
\q2 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb will shake|מַרְעִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,\f + \fr 2:6 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 12:26|HEB 12:26\ref*\f*
\q2 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the dry land|הֶחָרָבָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb I will shake|וְהִרְעַשְׁתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they will come|וּבָ֖אוּ\rb* \rb with all their treasures|חֶמְדַּ֣ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb and I will fill|וּמִלֵּאתִ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb* \rb with glory|כָּב֔וֹד\rb*,
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb The silver is|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb Mine|לִ֥י\rb*, \rb and the gold is|הַזָּהָ֑ב\rb* \rb Mine|וְלִ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb The latter|הָאַֽחֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb glory|כְּבוֹד֩\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֨יִת\rb*
\q2 \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶ֡ה\rb* \rb greater|גָּד֣וֹל\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the former|הָ֣רִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \rb And in this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb place|וּבַמָּק֤וֹם\rb* \rb I will provide|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb peace|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Blessings for a Defiled People
\p \v 10 \rb On the twenty-fourth day|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָה֙\rb* \rb of the ninth month|לַתְּשִׁיעִ֔י\rb*, \rb in the second|שְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Darius|לְדָרְיָ֑וֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֥י\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 11 “\rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb Ask|שְׁאַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֧א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb for a ruling|תּוֹרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb If|הֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb carries|יִשָּׂא־\rb* \rb consecrated|קֹ֜דֶשׁ\rb* \rb meat|בְּשַׂר־\rb* \rb in the fold|בִּכְנַ֣ף\rb* \rb of his garment|בִּגְד֗וֹ\rb*, \rb and it|בִּ֠כְנָפוֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb touches|וְנָגַ֣ע\rb* \rb bread|הַלֶּ֨חֶם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb stew|הַנָּזִ֜יד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb wine|הַיַּ֧יִן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֛מֶן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb or any|כָּל־\rb* \rb other food|מַאֲכָ֖ל\rb*, \rb does that item become holy|הֲיִקְדָּ֑שׁ\rb*?’”
\p “\rb No|לֹֽא׃\rb*,”\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּעֲנ֧וּ\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb So Haggai|חַגַּ֔י\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb one who is defiled|טְמֵא־\rb* \rb by contact with a corpse|נֶ֛פֶשׁ\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּ֧ע\rb* \rb any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb*, \rb does it become defiled|הֲיִטְמָ֑א\rb*?”
\p “\rb Yes, it becomes defiled|יִטְמָֽא׃\rb*,” \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּעֲנ֧וּ\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Then Haggai|חַגַּ֜י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb So it is|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb with this|הַ֠זֶּה\rb* \rb people|הָֽעָם־\rb* \rb and|וְכֵן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֨וֹי\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַי֙\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and so it is|וְכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb with every|כָּל־\rb* \rb work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb whatever|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they offer|יַקְרִ֛יבוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb is defiled|טָמֵ֥א\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*\rb |שִֽׂימוּ־\rb* \rb consider|לְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb carefully|נָ֣א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb forward|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb*:\f + \fr 2:15 \ft Or \fqa backward\ft ; also in verse 18\f* \rb Before|מִטֶּ֧רֶם\rb* \rb one stone|אֶ֛בֶן\rb* \rb was placed|שֽׂוּם־\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|אֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb in the temple|בְּהֵיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb from that time|מִֽהְיוֹתָ֥ם\rb*, \rb when one came|בָּא֙\rb* \rb expecting|אֶל־\rb* \rb a heap|עֲרֵמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of twenty ephahs of grain|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Literally \fqa a heap of twenty\f* \rb there were|וְהָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb but ten|עֲשָׂרָ֑ה\rb*. \rb When one came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the winepress|הַיֶּ֗קֶב\rb* \rb to draw out|לַחְשֹׂף֙\rb* \rb fifty baths|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |פּוּרָ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Literally \fqa to draw out fifty from the winepress\f* \rb there were|וְהָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb but twenty|עֶשְׂרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb I struck you|הִכֵּ֨יתִי\rb*—\rb |אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of your hands|יְדֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*— \rb with blight|בַּשִּׁדָּפ֤וֹן\rb*, \rb mildew|וּבַיֵּֽרָקוֹן֙\rb*, \rb and hail|וּבַבָּרָ֔ד\rb*,\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb but you did not|וְאֵין־\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb turn to Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Consider carefully|שִׂימוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb*\rb |לְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb forward|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* — \rb from|לְמִן־\rb* \rb the twenty-fourth|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֜ה\rb* \rb day|מִיּוֹם֩\rb* \rb of the ninth month|לַתְּשִׁיעִ֗י\rb*, \rb the day|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the foundation of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb temple|הֵֽיכַל־\rb* \rb was laid|יֻסַּ֥ד\rb* — \rb consider carefully|שִׂ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |לְבַבְכֶֽם׃\rb*: \v 19 \rb Is there still|הַע֤וֹד\rb* \rb seed|הַזֶּ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb in the barn|בַּמְּגוּרָ֔ה\rb*? \rb The vine|הַגֶּ֨פֶן\rb*, \rb the fig|וְהַתְּאֵנָ֧ה\rb*, \rb the pomegranate|וְהָרִמּ֛וֹן\rb*, \rb and the olive|הַזַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb tree|וְעֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb yet|וְעַד־\rb* \rb yielded fruit|נָשָׂ֑א\rb*. \rb But from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb day on|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb I will bless you|אֲבָרֵֽךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 Zerubbabel the LORD’s Signet Ring
\p \v 20 \rb For the second time that day|שֵׁנִית֙\rb*, \rb the twenty-fourth|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֛ה\rb* \rb day of the month|לַחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֔י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 21 “\rb Tell|אֱמֹ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֥ל\rb* \rb governor|פַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am about to shake|מַרְעִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb I will overturn|וְהָֽפַכְתִּי֙\rb* \rb royal|מַמְלָכ֔וֹת\rb* \rb thrones|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb*
\q2 \rb and destroy|וְהִ֨שְׁמַדְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb the power|חֹ֖זֶק\rb*
\q2 \rb of the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will overturn|וְהָפַכְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb chariots|מֶרְכָּבָה֙\rb* \rb and their riders|וְרֹ֣כְבֶ֔יהָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb horses|סוּסִים֙\rb* \rb and their riders|וְרֹ֣כְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will fall|וְיָרְד֤וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb by the sword|בְּחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb of his brother|אָחִֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb On that|הַה֣וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֡וֹת\rb*,
\q1 \rb I will take you|אֶ֠קָּחֲךָ\rb*, \rb My servant|עַבְדִּי֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֨ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שְׁאַלְתִּיאֵ֤ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb and I will make you|וְשַׂמְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb like My signet ring|כַּֽחוֹתָ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have chosen|בָחַ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb you|בְךָ֣\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*.”
